        "1": {
          "evidence": "At the 2020.0 vertical gridline, the blue circular marker is located in the upper half of the plot area, while the red square marker is located at the very bottom of the plot area. The blue mark is substantially higher than the red mark.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "The vertical text on the left y-axis reads 'Rest of the world' in blue. The vertical text on the right y-axis reads 'U.S.' in red.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "3": {
          "evidence": "Numerical labels are visible for the 2018 and 2019 data points: '13993' (blue) and '15875' (red) at 2018.0; '14272' (blue) and '16194' (red) at 2019.0.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the blue Rest of the world series and red U.S. series use vertically comparable 2020 value scales, then the series whose 2020 mark is higher on the plot has the larger reported value; the task directs opening that region's follow-up record.",
        "evidence": "The reading requires two conditions: (1) that the colored axis labels bind blue to 'Rest of the world' and red to 'U.S.', and (2) that the two vertically separated axes are comparable for ranking the 2020 values. Condition (1) is supported by the visual evidence (blue text on left, red text on right). Condition (2) is the critical applicability test. The chart uses a dual-axis layout with no numerical tick labels or units printed on either axis. The 2018 and 2019 data points show that the red (U.S.) series has higher values (15875, 16194) than the blue (Rest of the world) series (13993, 14272), yet the red marks are plotted lower than the blue marks in those years. This indicates the two axes have different scales and are not vertically comparable for direct ranking. Therefore, the condition that the axes are comparable is refuted by the chart's own data. The relative vertical position of the 2020 marks cannot be used to determine which value is larger.",
        "status": "refuted"
      }
    }
  }
}
